# A matrix: a rectangular grid of numbers, the concrete shape of a linear map between vector spaces once bases are
# chosen. Multiplying matrices composes the maps, and the rotations of the eight-dimensional arena are the orthogonal
# matrices whose structure gives the Lie algebra D4. The form carries the row and column counts and an opaque store of
# entries; the multiplication and its compatibility with dimensions are developed where matrices are used.
form matrix
  link rows, like natural
  link columns, like natural
  link entries, note private
